codex
Implemented and verified the problem generator based on Section 4.3 of [Parameterized Complexity of Vehicle Routing](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10361).

Shipping configuration: `medium`, with 48 routes and 144 clients.

Key results:

- Planted witnesses: 8/8 verified
- Corruptions: 5/5 rejected with distinct reasons
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000
- Adversary attacks: 0/8 successes each
- Canonical invariance: 60/60
- Oracle verdict: `hardened` at medium, zero escalations

Deliverables:

- [gen_2509_10361.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2509.10361/gen_2509_10361.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2509.10361/selftest_report.json)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2509.10361/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2509.10361/README.md)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2509.10361/.meta.json)

The README records the important caveat that only one oracle produced a checked-but-invalid witness; the other two exhausted or ended their response budgets without emitting answers.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
